    "Full API spec": "Build: pom.xml\n- Declares Java 11 source/target. Dependency: org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter (test scope). Plugin: maven-surefire-plugin configured for JUnit 5. No other dependencies. Test command: mvn -q test.\n\nsrc/main/java/ProcessingReport.java:\n- public final class ProcessingReport\n  - private int rowsRead, rowsKept, rowsWritten initialized to 0.\n  - private LinkedHashMap<String,Integer> invalidCounts initialized empty.\n  - public ProcessingReport()\n  - public void incrementRowsRead(): increments rowsRead by exactly 1.\n  - public void incrementRowsKept(): increments rowsKept by exactly 1.\n  - public void incrementRowsWritten(): increments rowsWritten by exactly 1.\n  - public void recordInvalid(String column): adds 1 to invalidCounts for key column exactly once per call; must not increment other counters.\n  - public int getRowsRead(), getRowsKept(), getRowsWritten(): return respective counters.\n  - public LinkedHashMap<String,Integer> invalidCounts(): returns an unmodifiable defensive copy preserving insertion order. No method changes unrelated counters.\n\nsrc/main/java/Cell.java:\n- public final class Cell\n  - private final String raw.\n  - public static Cell of(String raw): if raw==null, store empty string; else store raw as-is.\n  - public String raw(): returns stored raw.\n  - public boolean isBlank(): returns raw.trim().isEmpty(). Immutable; no setters.\n\nsrc/main/java/Row.java:\n- public final class Row\n  - private final List<String> header; private final List<Cell> cells; both copied defensively in constructor.\n  - public Row(List<String> header, List<Cell> cells): copies inputs and may pad internal cells to header size using Cell.of(\"\") if needed.\n  - public List<String> header(): returns unmodifiable defensive copy or unmodifiable view that cannot be mutated by caller.\n  - public List<Cell> cells(): returns unmodifiable defensive view of cells list.\n  - public Cell get(String column): finds first index i in header with header.get(i).equals(column); if found and i < cells.size(), return cells.get(i); if not found or i>=cells.size(), return Cell.of(\"\").\n  - public LinkedHashMap<String,String> asStringMap(): builds an ordered map of header->cells[i].raw() for each header index; if cells shorter, empty string for missing.\n\nsrc/main/java/Sorters.java:\n- public final class Sorters\n  - public static final class Order\n    - private final String column; private final boolean ascending.\n    - public Order(String column, boolean ascending)\n    - public String column(): returns column.\n    - public boolean ascending(): returns ascending.\n  - public static Comparator<Row> comparator(List<Order> orders): returns a comparator that for each Order compares the corresponding Cell.raw() strings; blanks (cell.isBlank()) always sort after non-blanks regardless of ascending/descending; for non-blank comparisons use String.compareTo; apply ascending flag by reversing sign if needed; if tie across all orders, deterministically tie-break by comparing full Row as concatenated raw strings (e.g., iterate header order) to avoid nondeterminism; never use Java streams.\n\nsrc/main/java/Sheet.java:\n- public final class Sheet\n  - private final String name; private final List<String> header; private final List<Row> rows.\n  - public Sheet(String name, List<String> header, List<Row> rows): copies inputs defensively.\n  - public String name(): returns name.\n  - public List<String> header(): unmodifiable defensive header view.\n  - public List<Row> rows(): unmodifiable defensive rows view.\n  - public Sheet filter(Predicate<Row> predicate, ProcessingReport report): builds a new Sheet with only rows where predicate.test(row) is true; for each retained row, call report.incrementRowsKept() exactly once; does not change report.rowsRead or rowsWritten; header/name preserved.\n  - public Sheet sort(List<Sorters.Order> orders): returns a new Sheet with rows sorted by Sorters.comparator(orders); no counter changes.\n\nsrc/main/java/Workbook.java:\n- public final class Workbook\n  - private final LinkedHashMap<String, Sheet> sheets = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n  - public Workbook()\n  - public void addSheet(Sheet sheet): inserts/overwrites by sheet.name().\n  - public Optional<Sheet> getSheet(String name): returns Optional.of(sheet) if present, else Optional.empty().\n  - public Set<String> sheetNames(): returns unmodifiable defensive set copy preserving insertion order if applicable.\n\nsrc/main/java/ValueParser.java:\n- public final class ValueParser\n  - public static Double toDouble(String raw, String column, ProcessingReport report): if raw==null or raw.trim().isEmpty(), return null without recording; else attempt Double.valueOf(trimmed); on NumberFormatException, call report.recordInvalid(column) exactly once and return null.\n\nsrc/main/java/Filters.java:\n- public final class Filters\n  - public static Predicate<Row> equals(String column, String value): returns predicate evaluating row.get(column).raw().equals(value).\n  - public static Predicate<Row> contains(String column, String fragment): returns predicate evaluating row.get(column).raw().contains(fragment).\n  - public static Predicate<Row> numericGreaterThan(String column, double threshold, ProcessingReport report): for a given row, call ValueParser.toDouble once with row.get(column).raw(); if null return false; else return parsed > threshold.\n\nsrc/main/java/Aggregations.java:\n- public final class Aggregations\n  - public static int count(Sheet sheet): returns sheet.rows().size().\n  - public static double sum(Sheet sheet, String column, ProcessingReport report): iterate rows once, call ValueParser.toDouble once per row; accumulate non-null values; ignore blanks/invalids; return 0.0 if none.\n  - public static double average(Sheet sheet, String column, ProcessingReport report): as sum but divide by count of numeric values; return 0.0 if no numeric values.\n  - public static Double min(Sheet sheet, String column, ProcessingReport report): iterate once, call ValueParser once per row; track smallest non-null; return null if none.\n  - public static Double max(Sheet sheet, String column, ProcessingReport report): iterate once, call ValueParser once per row; track largest non-null; return null if none.\n  - All methods must not use Java streams; use for loops and ArrayList.\n\nsrc/main/java/CsvIO.java:\n- public final class CsvIO\n  - public static Sheet importCsvFromString(String name, String csv, ProcessingReport report): split by '\\n' retaining order; first line is header split by ',' with negative limit to preserve trailing empties; for each subsequent line (data row), split with negative limit; pad to header length with empty strings; ignore excess cells; construct Cell for each field; wrap in Row; increment report.incrementRowsRead() exactly once per data row; return new Sheet(name, header, dataRows).\n  - public static String toCsvString(Sheet sheet, ProcessingReport report): build string with header line (comma-joined) followed by each row as comma-joined cell.raw(); for every data row written, call report.incrementRowsWritten() exactly once; must not modify rowsRead or rowsKept; use '\\n' line separators; do not quote commas or escape.\n\nsrc/main/java/Main.java:\n- public final class Main\n  - public static void main(String[] args): prepare a fixed in-memory CSV string; use fresh ProcessingReport for each phase (import, filter, aggregation, export); invoke CsvIO.importCsvFromString, Sheet.filter, Sheet.sort, Aggregations.sum, CsvIO.toCsvString; print one concise deterministic summary; no input, no filesystem/network, no randomness, no threads, no streams.\n\nsrc/test/java/MainTest.java:\n- JUnit 5 tests only; default package; imports only org.junit.jupiter.api.Test and static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.* plus java.util.*; refer to project classes by simple names; no explicit project imports.\n- Exactly three tests:\n  1) runtime invokes Main.main(new String[0]) returns normally.\n  2) three-row pipeline uses literal CSV `Name,Country,Sales\\nAlice,US,1000\\nBob,CA,1500\\nCharlie,US,2000`; import with fresh reportImport assert rowsRead==3; filter Country==\"US\" with fresh reportFilter assert rowsKept==2; literally assert `assertEquals(\"Alice\", filteredRows.get(0).get(\"Name\").raw());` and `assertEquals(\"Charlie\", filteredRows.get(1).get(\"Name\").raw());`; sort those rows descending by Name and literally assert `assertEquals(\"Charlie\", sortedRows.get(0).get(\"Name\").raw());` and `assertEquals(\"Alice\", sortedRows.get(1).get(\"Name\").raw());`; sum Sales with fresh reportAggregation assert 3000.0 and invalidCounts empty.\n  3) invalid/round-trip uses literal CSV `Name,Sales\\nAlice,1000\\nBob,bad\\nCharlie,\\nDana,2000`; call sum exactly once with fresh reportAggregation assert 3000.0 and invalidCounts().get(\"Sales\")==1; export with fresh reportExport assert rowsWritten==4; re-import with fresh reportReimport assert rowsRead==4, identical header, four rows, and Bob's Sales remains `bad`.\n\nGlobal constraints:\n- All classes in default (unnamed) package; tests must not import project classes.\n- Java streams are forbidden across all files; use loops and ArrayList.\n- CsvIO exposes exactly two public static methods as specified; no overloads.\n- Each independent operation uses a fresh ProcessingReport; counters have precise ownership semantics.\n- Allowed dependency direction: ProcessingReport, Cell -> Row -> Sorters/Sheet -> Workbook/Filters/Aggregations/CsvIO -> Main -> MainTest. Tests call public APIs only.",
    "Shared Knowledge": "This repository is a headless Java 11 Maven project implementing in-memory Excel-like data processing with CSV import/export, filtering, sorting, and aggregations. All implementation classes live in the default package under src/main/java and are dependency-ordered. ProcessingReport owns counters and invalid counts; Cell and Row are immutable-like with defensive copies; Sorters provides multi-column comparator with blanks-last; Sheet performs filter and sort without mutating counters except rowsKept during filter; Workbook is an in-memory container; ValueParser provides numeric parsing with exact invalid recording semantics; Filters and Aggregations are pure rules calling ValueParser exactly once per visited row; CsvIO implements two static methods for CSV import/export with precise counter effects; Main demonstrates a fixed pipeline with fresh reports per phase; MainTest (JUnit 5) contains exactly three tests, imports only JUnit and java.util, references project classes by simple names in the unnamed package, and never uses Java streams.",
    "Execution Protocol": "Build and test with: mvn -q test. Runtime entry: src/main/java/Main.java (default package). Single protocol-level test target: src/test/java/MainTest.java with exactly three tests. Tests are deterministic, headless, offline, and non-interactive. No additional test files are present. No network, filesystem, clock, GUI, threads, or randomness are used.",
